    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T22:08:54Z",
    "body": "Thank you for the readings (1 failure in 3 parallel runs, 3 of 3 passes alone) and the suspected cause.\n\nTriage: `bug`, `P5` (a flaky test turns contributors' quick gates red at random), `effort:low`, `area:ui`. We do not set `source:agent` on issues from outside accounts.\n\nRelated: #2432 (merged today) isolated the live theme state between parallel UI unit tests, for the same class of problem (a test that reads shared global state while other tests run). The fix here is likely the same shape: the test should capture only its own events (a scoped subscriber or a per-test filter), not the process-wide tracing output. If you want to work on it, comment a line that starts with `claimed:`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
